issue.message:
Unexpected failure during lint analysis of AnimalsOnTop.kt (this is a bug in lint or one of the libraries it depends on)


The crash seems to involve the detector `com.greense.detector.mylibrary.NLMRDetector`.
You can try disabling it with something like this:
    android {
        lintOptions {
            disable "No Low Memory Resolver"
        }
    }

Stack: `NullPointerException:Objects.requireNonNull(Objects.java:222)←NLMRDetector.visitClass(NLMRDetector.java:35)←UElementVisitor$SuperclassPsiVisitor.checkClass(UElementVisitor.kt:465)←UElementVisitor$SuperclassPsiVisitor.visitClass(UElementVisitor.kt:441)←AbstractKotlinUClass.accept(KotlinUClass.kt:62)←ImplementationUtilsKt.acceptList(implementationUtils.kt:23)←UFile$DefaultImpls.accept(UFile.kt:97)←KotlinUFile.accept(KotlinUFile.kt:30)`

You can set environment variable `LINT_PRINT_STACKTRACE=true` to dump a full stacktrace to stdout.

